                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            are uniquely determined, and similarly for the transformations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ε
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon
          %p This completes the sketched proof of essential uniqueness.
          %h2#cartesian_bicategories_and_hyperdoctrines Cartesian bicategories and hyperdoctrines
          %p
            Each cartesian bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
